% A predicate derived by facts and rules alike is read on demand like any
% other, and its facts become rules guarded by its magic predicate, so that
% only the facts a call asks for are derived.  A predicate derived by facts
% alone is read as it is.

link(a, b).
link(b, c).
link(c, d).
link(p, q).
link(X, Z) :- link(X, Y), hop(Y, Z).
hop(c, z).
hop(q, r).

link(a, X)?
link(X, r)?
